{"id":"word:hebrew:H4069","type":"word","title":"מַדּוּעַ","subtitle":"H4069 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"what (is) known? ; i.e. (by implication) (adverbially) why?","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מַדּוּעַ (H4069) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: adv.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 72 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מַדּוּעַ (maddûwaʻ) means what (is) known? ; i.e. (by implication) (adverbially) why? First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 1 6."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מַדּוּעַ","transliteration":"maddûwaʻ","pronunciation":"mad-doo'-ah","strong":"H4069","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4069","partOfSpeech":"adv","forms":["מַדּ֖וּעַ","מַדּ֗וּעַ","מַדּוּעַ֩","מַדּ֛וּעַ","מַדּ֣וּעַ"],"morphs":[["HTi",62],["HC/Ti",9],["HC/D",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"what (is) known? ; i.e. (by implication) (adverbially) why?","usage":"how, wherefore, why.","full":"H4069. maddua מַדּוּעַ 61 and :( Exod 18:19 ) מַדֻּעַ adverb wherefore? (probably contracted from מַהיָּֿדוּעַ what being known ? i.e. from what motive? so Ges Ew §325 c Ol §223 f , compare in Greek τί μαθών ;) — wherefore? on what account ? Gen 26:27 אֵלָ֑י בָּאתֶם מַדּוּעַ , 40:7 ; Exod 1:18 ; 2:18 ; 3:8 (in an indirect question), 5:14 ; 18:14 ; Lev 10:17 ; Josh 17:14 (all in Hexateuch), Judg 5:28 (twice in verse); 2Sam 3:7 ; 11:10 etc., Isa 5:4 ; 50:2 ; 63:2 (all in Isaiah); in Jeremiah 16 t., oft, rhetorically, after a double question introduced by הֲאִ֗֗֗ם , expressing affected surprise: Jer 2:14 (see Gf) is Israel a slave (unable to defend himself)? wherefore , then, is he become a prey? (some other cause must therefore be found for Israel's misfortune), 2:31 ; 8:5 , 19 , 22 ; 14:19 ; 22:28 ; 49:1 , compare 30:6 ; Job 3:12 ; 18:8 (never in Psalms).","rootNote":"or מַדֻּעַ ; from 4100 and the passive participle of 3045 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-B